**Purpose**:
The purpose is to have only the actually updated orders on MDM.
**Approach**:
Diffing strategy before calling stage#ShopifyOrder so that mega query is called only for orders that are actually updated.
- The minimal information I am thinking of pulling from Shopify, before sending an order to the MDM:
    - No ShopifyOrderHistory exists
    - Header hash changed: email, phone, note, tags, customer, shipping/billing address
    - cancelledAt changed
    - displayFinancialStatus / displayFulfillmentStatus / returnStatus changed
    - line item id or quantity/currentQuantity changed
    - New fulfillment id exists
    - fulfillment updatedAt is newer than local history
    - New refund id exists
    - refund updatedAt is newer than local history
    - New transaction id exists
    - transaction status changed

**Reason for selecting these fields:**
1. Order create/update
    - No ShopifyOrderHistory means OMS may not have the order, so full fetch is needed.
    - Existing order update currently compares only: email, phone, note, tags, shippingAddress, billingAddress, customer, line item quantity
2. Fulfillment processing
    - It only checks whether a fulfillment ID is missing from ShopifyFulfillmentHistory.
3. Refund / return / exchange processing
    - It only checks whether a refund ID is missing from ShopifyRefundHistory.
    - refund/return payload then drives refund, return, exchange handling.
4. Transaction processing
    - It checks whether transaction IDs are missing from ShopifyTransactionHistory.

```text
orders(first: 100, after: $cursor, sortKey: UPDATED_AT, query: $queryString) {
  nodes {
    id
    legacyResourceId
    updatedAt
    email
    phone
    note
    tags
    cancelledAt
    displayFinancialStatus
    displayFulfillmentStatus
    returnStatus
    edited

    currentTotalPriceSet {
      shopMoney { amount currencyCode }
    }

    customer {
      id
      firstName
      lastName
    }

    shippingAddress {
      name address1 address2 city zip provinceCode countryCodeV2 phone
    }

    billingAddress {
      name address1 address2 city zip provinceCode countryCodeV2 phone
    }

    lineItems(first: 50) {
      nodes {
        id
        quantity
        currentQuantity
        unfulfilledQuantity
        nonFulfillableQuantity
      }
    }

    fulfillments(first: 10) {
      id
      updatedAt
      legacyResourceId
    }

    transactions {
      id
      kind
      status
      processedAt
    }

    refunds {
      id
      legacyResourceId
      createdAt
      updatedAt
      totalRefundedSet {
        shopMoney { amount currencyCode }
      }
      return {
        id
        status
        createdAt
        closedAt
        totalQuantity
      }
    }
  }

  pageInfo {
    hasNextPage
    endCursor
  }
}
```
